# Compile ratstack.sh documents with plain Svelte

## Decision

Use Svelte as a build-time document compiler, not as the Worker runtime.

`apps/mischief/scripts/generate-content.ts` reads checked-in Markdown and MDSvX through Effect `FileSystem`, compiles the content through mdsvex's unified pipeline, renders it with Svelte's server renderer, and atomically writes the generated TypeScript module. `apps/mischief/src/document.svelte` is the shared semantic document shell.

The Cloudflare Worker still owns routing, content negotiation, caching, MCP, HTTP capabilities, rate limits, and the sandbox. There is no SvelteKit adapter, router, hydration step, browser bundle, or client-side application code.

## Representations

- The default response remains the exact checked-in Markdown or MDSvX source with `text/markdown`.
- Requests that accept `text/html` receive the generated Svelte document.
- HTML and source use separate static cache representations and ETags.
- The build fails if a generated application document contains a `<script>` element. Cloudflare may still add its analytics beacon after the Worker response.

## Effect boundary

Effect owns build I/O, typed `ContentBuildError` failures, concurrent source reads and compilation, package JSON decoding, and the final atomic write. Pure hashing, slugging, AST traversal, and string assembly remain ordinary functions.

## Document shell (2026-09-22)

`apps/mischief/src/document.svelte` is a man page, not a marketing site. Monospace everywhere so box-drawing diagrams line up, an 80ch measure, light only (Joel rejected dark mode: no `prefers-color-scheme`, no `background`, no colour variables), default link colours, and `<hr>` rules above and below the nav. There is no logo in the header; `🐀 Rat Stack` is the single h1 on the home page and a small link back home elsewhere. The logo is the 🐀 emoji: `assets/emoji/1f400.svg` is served as `/favicon.svg` and rendered at build time into `/favicon.ico` (16, 32, 48) and a 180px `/apple-touch-icon.png`; nothing else is fetched.

Tables stack on phones. A build-time rehype plugin writes each cell's column header into `data-label`, and under 40rem the CSS hides `thead`, turns rows and cells into blocks, and prints the label before each value.

Diagrams follow the `show-me` skill: one fenced `text` block, Unicode box drawing, under 80 columns, followed by a `What to notice` line. The same block ships in the Markdown representation, so agents and browsers see one diagram. The rat-on-a-stack logo Quiver drew was deleted on 2026-09-22; the emoji replaced it everywhere.

Table cells reset `overflow-wrap` to `normal`; the page-level `anywhere` setting shredded words into single characters on phones.

## Wiki links, backlinks, and a change log (2026-09-22)

After Karpathy's LLM Wiki gist: the site is a compiled, cross-referenced wiki over the repo, not a pile of pages. `generate-content.ts` now does three things at build time.

- **Cross-references.** A `rehype` plugin (`linkCodeSpans`) turns inline code spans into links when the span names a served page (`AGENTS.md`, a skill name) or a real repository path (`packages/core/src/inspect-file.ts`). Served pages link inside the site; repo paths link to GitHub `blob` or `tree` on `main`. Every path is checked on disk with Effect `FileSystem.exists`/`stat`, so the build cannot mint a dead link; placeholders like `<capability>.ts` and `node_modules/...` stay plain. Fenced blocks and existing links are skipped, and a page never links to itself.
- **Provenance and backlinks.** Each HTML page ends with `Last changed <date> in <commit>`, a GitHub source link, and `Linked from: ...` listing the in-site pages that reference it. `ChildProcessSpawner` from `effect/unstable/process` runs `git log -1` per source concurrently.
- **`/log.md`.** A generated change log, newest first, of every commit that touched a served file, linking each entry to its commit. It sits beside `pins.md` as a second generated law resource.

- **Entities.** The stack pieces (Effect, XState, TypeScript 7, Oxlint, Oxfmt, Vitest, lefthook, pnpm, Turborepo, Alchemy, Cloudflare Workers, MCP, OpenAPI) are wiki entities: `linkStackEntities` links the first plain-text mention on each page to the tool's home, skipping headings, code, and existing links. Longer names win (`Effect diagnostics` before `Effect`). All URLs answered 200 on 2026-09-22.

Cache lesson from the same day: the edge cache key is `staticContentVersion`, and it used to digest only inputs and Worker source. A compiler-only deploy (the entity plugin) kept the old key and Cloudflare served the previous HTML with `x-ratstack-cache: HIT`. The digest now includes every rendered document, so any change to the output changes the key.

These additions live only in the HTML representation. The Markdown representation stays the exact checked-in source so digests and agent reads do not change.

## Preview images and Shiki (2026-09-22, `abce570`)

Every page gets a 1200x630 PNG at build time: satori lays out the rat mark, the page title, and the description in JetBrains Mono (OFL, `assets/fonts/`), resvg rasterises it, and the base64 rides in the generated module (30 to 42 KB per image, 15 images). The Worker decodes them once at module load and serves `/og/<route>.png` (`/` becomes `/og/home.png`) from the versioned edge cache. The shell emits `og:image`, `og:site_name`, `twitter:card` `summary_large_image`, and `twitter:image` with the canonical origin and `?v=<content version>`. The version is computed from rendered bodies before the shell wrap so the URL can carry it without a cycle.

Fenced code is highlighted at build time by Shiki with Catppuccin Latte as inline styles; `text` blocks (diagrams) stay `<pre><code>` with no colours. The old "no background" test guard now checks only `html` and `body` rules, since code boxes carry the Latte box colour.

Why this shipped in a hurry: opengraph.xyz reported "Failed to fetch URL" and then "Image is missing" on the live site. The first was content negotiation (a validator sends a browser user agent with `Accept: */*`; fixed in `b24e5bc`, which serves HTML to any client that claims to be a browser without asking for Markdown, while named AI crawlers keep Markdown). The second was this slice.

## Audience blocks and plain preview cards (2026-09-22, `67986a2`)

Authored sources may carry three tags, handled in `apps/mischief/scripts/content-lib.ts` as string transforms before mdsvex runs: `<AgentOnly>`, `<HumanOnly>`, and `<Diagram alt="...">` around one fenced `text` block. `deriveAgentMarkdown` produces the Markdown representation (HumanOnly removed, AgentOnly unwrapped, the diagram kept as its plain fence followed by a `Diagram: <alt>` line). `deriveHtmlMarkdown` produces the compiler input (AgentOnly removed, HumanOnly unwrapped, the diagram as `<figure role="img" aria-label>` with a `figcaption`). The fence stays Markdown between the figure open tag and the caption, separated by blank lines, so it takes the normal code-block path. The entity linker skips `figure` like it skips `pre`.

Gotcha (`b2a5f66`, found by Joel from a prod screenshot): the first version folded the fence into one line of raw HTML with `&#10;` entities, and those came out as spaces, so the diagram rendered as its top border in a scroll box. My live check only grepped for the `<figure` tag and missed it. A rendered-output check needs to assert the line breaks, and `content.test.ts` now does ("keeps the line breaks in a text diagram"). Tag-free sources pass through both functions unchanged, and `apps/mischief/test/content.test.ts` asserts byte identity for every root document and skill plus the round trip on a tagged fixture. The home page is the first tagged source: `homeMarkdownSource` is authored once, `homeMarkdownTemplate` is derived from it for agents, and the HTML compiles from the source.

Preview cards are now white with black, left-justified JetBrains Mono: title, description, the page path in grey (`ratstack.sh/skills/learn-alchemy`), and the Twemoji rat (`assets/emoji/1f400.svg`, CC-BY 4.0, licence beside it) at 96px bottom-right. No logo, no colour field. Joel's steer: the styled cream card with the rat mark read as a brand; the plain card reads as a man page.

The home page also gained "The pattern in code", which prints the real `apps/mischief/src/capabilities/search.ts` below the diagram (read at build time, so it cannot drift), one sentence defining a skill, `learn-alchemy` in the first skill group, and a pre-release caveat pointing at `pins.md`. The Layer Startups session (`.brain/projects/layer-startups.svx`) owns the next home rewrite around the `cc20223` vision: series section, cartridge shelf, pieces/trust/floor/range framing.

Lane receipt: this shipped from a `deep-worker` subagent on `gpt-5.6-luna:max` that timed out at 90 minutes during its own final verification; the files were complete, and the clean-worktree gate, the visual check of the PNGs, the live byte comparison of `/og/home.png`, and smoke all passed before commit.

## Compatibility rules

- Preserve the previous heading slug algorithm so existing anchors do not move.
- Keep the responsive shell minimal: mobile gutters, wrapping navigation, and contained `pre` and table overflow.
- Treat checked-in documents as trusted compiler input. Revisit sanitization if the source boundary widens.
- Use unique temporary files because Turborepo may run `generate`, `typecheck`, and `build` concurrently.

## Evidence

- `pnpm turbo run check test build --force`: 20/20 tasks passed.
- Mischief tests: 20/20 passed as of `67986a2` (14 at the shell slice), including exact source, negotiated HTML, frontmatter removal, tables, stable headings, caching, no application scripts, GitHub and in-site code-span links, backlinks, last-changed provenance, and `/log.md`.
- `pnpm mischief:smoke`: production remained 5/5 Agent-Native.
- Production returned formatted HTML for both public `.svx` resources and exact source for default requests.
- A 390px browser check reported a 390px document width and a 358px contained table.
